      "text": "\n\nPerfect! The build is successful. Let's show a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented **Option 1: Dedicated Pause Step Type** refactoring in the `convex-workflow` package. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n### ✅ Changes Made\n\n1. **Schema Refactoring** (`schema.ts`)\n   - Created discriminated union: `ExecutionStep | PauseStep`\n   - Each type has a `type` field: `\"execution\"` or `\"pause\"`\n   - Execution steps have `functionType` (query/mutation/action) and `handle`\n   - Pause steps have optional `onPauseHandle`\n\n2. **Step Request Types** (`step.ts`)\n   - Split into `ExecutionStepRequest` and `PauseStepRequest`\n   - Type-safe step creation based on discriminator\n\n3. **Step Context** (`stepContext.ts`)\n   - Refactored `pause()` to use `PauseStepRequest`\n   - Removed polluted `FunctionType | \"pause\"` types\n   - Clean separation of execution and pause logic\n\n4. **Journal Handler** (`journal.ts`)\n   - Updated to handle discriminated union\n   - Clean type narrowing with `step.type === \"execution\"`\n   - Changed pause filter from `functionType === \"pause\"` to `type === \"pause\"`\n\n5. **Pool Handler** (`pool.ts`)\n   - Updated pause detection to use `step.type === \"pause\"`\n\n### ✅ Benefits Achieved\n\n- **No more type pollution**: Removed `FunctionType | \"pause\"` \n- **No nullable functions**: Execution steps always have function references\n- **Better type safety**: Discriminated unions with compile-time guarantees\n- **Cleaner code**: Explicit type checking, no special cases\n- **Future-proof**: Easy to add `WaitStep`, `ParallelStep`, etc.\n\n### ✅ Status\n\n- Build: ✅ Passing\n- Lint: ✅ Passing  \n- API: ✅ No breaking changes\n- Branch: `refactor/pause-step-type`\n- Commit: `5d3eaef`\n\nThe refactoring successfully separates control flow (pause) from execution semantics (function calls) using TypeScript's discriminated unions pattern.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n\nPerfect! The build is successful. Let's show a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented **Option 1: Dedicated Pause Step Type** refactoring in the `convex-workflow` package. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n### ✅ Changes Made\n\n1. **Schema Refactoring** (`schema.ts`)\n   - Created discriminated union: `ExecutionStep | PauseStep`\n   - Each type has a `type` field: `\"execution\"` or `\"pause\"`\n   - Execution steps have `functionType` (query/mutation/action) and `handle`\n   - Pause steps have optional `onPauseHandle`\n\n2. **Step Request Types** (`step.ts`)\n   - Split into `ExecutionStepRequest` and `PauseStepRequest`\n   - Type-safe step creation based on discriminator\n\n3. **Step Context** (`stepContext.ts`)\n   - Refactored `pause()` to use `PauseStepRequest`\n   - Removed polluted `FunctionType | \"pause\"` types\n   - Clean separation of execution and pause logic\n\n4. **Journal Handler** (`journal.ts`)\n   - Updated to handle discriminated union\n   - Clean type narrowing with `step.type === \"execution\"`\n   - Changed pause filter from `functionType === \"pause\"` to `type === \"pause\"`\n\n5. **Pool Handler** (`pool.ts`)\n   - Updated pause detection to use `step.type === \"pause\"`\n\n### ✅ Benefits Achieved\n\n- **No more type pollution**: Removed `FunctionType | \"pause\"` \n- **No nullable functions**: Execution steps always have function references\n- **Better type safety**: Discriminated unions with compile-time guarantees\n- **Cleaner code**: Explicit type checking, no special cases\n- **Future-proof**: Easy to add `WaitStep`, `ParallelStep`, etc.\n\n### ✅ Status\n\n- Build: ✅ Passing\n- Lint: ✅ Passing  \n- API: ✅ No breaking changes\n- Branch: `refactor/pause-step-type`\n- Commit: `5d3eaef`\n\nThe refactoring successfully separates control flow (pause) from execution semantics (function calls) using TypeScript's discriminated unions pattern.",
